Fix the SC_NO_THREADING build.

Upstream advertises SC_NO_THREADING=ON as a supported configuration, and PLAN D4/P02.7 needs
it: the fallback artifact for browsers and hosts that cannot deliver cross-origin isolation,
where SharedArrayBuffer and therefore emscripten pthreads are unavailable.

At c015720 that configuration does not compile. The profileset HTML/text/chart reporting code
reaches into profileset types that only exist in a threaded build (profileset.hpp declares
statistical_data_t and profile_set_t as incomplete types under SC_NO_THREADING), and
profileset.cpp's no-threading stub block defines profilesets_t::output_html/output_text, which
match no declaration in the header — dead code from an earlier refactor.

This guards the reporting paths that cannot exist without threading and deletes the two
undeclared stubs. It changes nothing in a threaded build: every hunk is inside
#ifndef SC_NO_THREADING or removes code that is only compiled when SC_NO_THREADING is set.

Not sent upstream from here — it is a build fix for a configuration we depend on, and the
project does not fork simc. If it is upstreamed, drop this file and bump engine.lock.json.

Applied by scripts/build-engine.sh --fallback only, and reversed when the build finishes.
